WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.161 --> 00:00:01.830
- All right y'all, before we say goodbye,

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:04.440
let's take a quick dive into
the world of social media.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.656
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:05.656 --> 00:00:08.490
(upbeat music)
(audience clapping)

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.220
So earlier, the cast of
"Shucked" impressed us all

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.390
with their vocal talents.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:15.210
It was so amazing, but there
is another little Broadway star

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:18.360
impressing people online,
this time through crocheting.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.193
I know.

00:00:19.193 --> 00:00:21.030
This is 12-year-old Michael.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:24.060
His crafting skills are
the star of his Instagram.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:27.000
He crochets everything from
shirts to blankets to hats,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.400
and you will never guess who taught him.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.730
Tony award-winning Broadway
actress Sutton Foster

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:35.010
actually taught him to crochet,
which I think is amazing.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.290
Let's get this little
crochet star in here.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:40.482
Watching on NBC New York,
say hi to Michael, everybody.

00:00:40.482 --> 00:00:43.596
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:43.596 --> 00:00:45.551
What's up, Michael?

00:00:45.551 --> 00:00:47.297
- Hi Kelly, how are you?

00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:50.880
- Oh my God, I am so excited.
Did you make your shirt?

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:51.713
- Yes, I did.

00:00:51.713 --> 00:00:53.700
I actually made it in a movie this summer

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:54.990
before the strike.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.360
- Oh, you look so great. Oh my gosh.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.370
So, Sutton Foster taught you, right?

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:00.780
Like, how did that happen?

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:03.540
- So, I was on "Music Man"
on Broadway last year,

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:06.120
and backstage we were all
a little rambunctious.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.910
So Sutton Foster, the legendary actress,

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:10.440
taught us how to crochet.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.870
And I always remember this one time

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:14.460
where I crocheted this blanket.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.040
It was wonky, it was horrible,
I don't even know what I did,

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.010
but I took it to Sutton
and she was so proud

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:20.880
and she said it was great.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.880
But then when I got home,
I really looked at it,

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:28.140
and I was like, "This woman
deserves a Tony, an Oscar."

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:29.670
She was the best actress I knew

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:33.690
because that blanket
was horrible. (laughs)

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:36.960
- No, I will say one time
I gave some of the coaches

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.540
at "The Voice," when I worked
on there, quilts that I made.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.450
They were sad if you looked closely.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.120
But if you were far
away, it was like, "Oh."

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.190
So we have one of Michael's pieces.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:50.130
This is a cardigan that he
crocheted and I wanted to...

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:51.750
This is so cool.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:53.460
How long did this take?

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.500
- So it took around four to five days,

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.540
but the challenge was like the design.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:00.810
So I chose that hot pink because
it fits your personality.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:03.090
You're sassy, fun, and I chose-

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:04.680
- Wait, what do you mean my personality?

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.150
Is this for me?

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:06.983
- Yes.

00:02:06.983 --> 00:02:08.510
- Oh!
(audience applauding)

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:09.343
- Yeah.

00:02:10.286 --> 00:02:12.600
- Well, thank you.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:15.030
- And if you look on the back, it says-

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.590
- Oh.
- MC X KC

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:18.690
'cause that's the ultimate collab.

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:20.940
- Oh, I love it.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.470
This is so sweet.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:23.490
I'm gonna wear this around here.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:24.990
Oh, it's right there. (gasps)

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:26.850
I love you so much, Michael.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:28.899
Thank you so much.
- I love you too.

00:02:28.899 --> 00:02:29.872
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:02:29.872 --> 00:02:31.800
- All right, everybody.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.200
So Michael, I'm liking
your post right now,

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.060
but that's not all, okay?

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.020
Our season-long...

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:39.480
Oh, this is cozy and warm. All right, son.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:41.220
Okay, our season-long partner-
- Thank you.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:42.510
- Pilot Pen, makers of FriXion,

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.610
the go-to erasable pen of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:47.790
want to celebrate those creating
fearlessly, just like you,

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.023
so they're gonna give you
$1,000 just for being rad.

00:02:50.023 --> 00:02:52.677
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:02:52.677 --> 00:02:54.870
- Thank you so much.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:56.010
- And your shirt is so cool.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:58.230
That sweater's so cool, man.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.790
Thank you so much, Michael.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.569
Thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:03:01.569 --> 00:03:06.264
Mario Lopez, Shane McAnally,
Grey Henson, John Behlmann,

00:03:06.264 --> 00:03:08.532
the cast of "Shucked," they're incredible.

00:03:08.532 --> 00:03:12.227
Dave, hilarious, Annie
Starke and Lawrence Zarian.

00:03:12.227 --> 00:03:15.082
Y'all have a great day and
until tomorrow, (indistinct).

